{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.U1EquivariantReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.U1EquivariantReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Instances.Real.Lemmas"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.phaseFiber_polar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.phaseFiber_polar","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/u1-equivariant-reduction.lean#L59-L64","doc":"The polar fixed-point fibre is `Unit` (collapsed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhaseFiber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhaseFiber","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/u1-equivariant-reduction.lean#L39-L57","doc":"**U(1)-equivariant reduction** (structural statement).\n`PhaseFiber φ` is:\n  - `Unit` at the two polar fixed points (φ = 0 or φ = π),\n    reflecting the collapse of the S¹ orbit to a point;\n  - intended to be `S¹` over the open interior (0, π).\n\nThis file records the signature only; the full bundle-theoretic\nformalisation (connection to `Mathlib.Topology.FiberBundle`) is\ndeferred.  The honest content here is the *structural asymmetry*\nbetween polar and interior points.\n\n`polarFixedPoints` is membership in a set cut out by real-number\nequalities (`x.val = 0 ∨ x.val = Real.pi`), which is not\nalgorithmically decidable; the case split is justified classically,\nhence the `Classical` instance and `noncomputable`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.polarFixedPoints","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.polarFixedPoints","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/u1-equivariant-reduction.lean#L29-L37","doc":"The polar fixed points of the U(1) action: φ = 0 and φ = π.\nThese are the two points where the U(1)-orbit on 𝒮_p collapses\nto a single point.\n\nFor `x : U1OrbitSpace`, `x.val : ℝ` is the underlying real number\n(the wrapper around a real carrying the Icc membership proof). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.U1OrbitSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.U1OrbitSpace","kind":"def","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/u1-equivariant-reduction.lean#L20-L27","doc":"Orbit space of the U(1) rotation action on the exceptional divisor\n𝒮_p = ℙ¹(ℂ), parametrised by the polar angle φ ∈ [0, π].\n\n`↥` is the subtype coercion: `U1OrbitSpace` is a `Type` whose\nelements are real numbers carrying a proof that they lie in\n`[0, π]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}